# API Route Handlers

## Standard flow
1. Auth guard (`getAdminUser()` or `supabase.auth.getUser()`)
2. `await request.json()` in try/catch → 400 on invalid JSON
3. Validate with Zod (`safeParse`) → 400 with `{ error, issues? }`
4. Mutate via appropriate Supabase client
5. Return `NextResponse.json(...)` with correct status

## Status codes used in this project
- 400 — validation / bad input
- 401 — not authenticated or not admin
- 409 — stock/product availability conflict (orders)
- 500 — unexpected DB errors
- 503 — Supabase not configured

## Orders (`/api/orders`)
- Never trust client prices — always re-fetch from DB
- Validate stock server-side before insert
- Emails are best-effort (`Promise.allSettled`) — never fail the order on email errors

## Uploads (`/api/admin/upload`)
- Max 5MB; only JPEG, PNG, WebP, AVIF
- Bucket: `product-images`; return `{ url: publicUrl }`
